                             => +1\\n#            x0=3: 11->2->1                
                             needs 2 steps => no\\n#                            
                             x0=4:100->1 => +1\\n#                              
                             x0=5:101->2->1 (2 steps) => no\\n#                 
                             x0=6:110->2->1 (2 steps) => no\\n#   so            
                             count_A=3\\n#   count_B=0 since                    
                             m=7<800\\n#   returns 3\\n\\n# The                 
                             large test case with m = 2^11-1 = 2047             
                             and k=1, they expect 800, which                    
                             suggests that all numbers with highest             
                             bit set (>=1024) and with popcount=1               
                             (i.e., 1024, but 1024>2047? no 1024 is             
                             within 2047) actually 1024 is 2^10, but            
